 After all chapters merge, a **full-book continuity audit** runs before final review. The auditor processes every chapter sequentially, building a cumulative world state and flagging long-range contradictions, unresolved plot threads, and accumulated drift that per-chapter checks can't catch. Results are compiled into `notes/continuity-audit-report.md`.
 
+### Release Phase
+
+Final review hands the finished manuscript to the release phase instead of ending the run. The **packager** assembles `manuscript/manuscript.md` plus a `release/manifest.json` (project status `PACKAGING`), then the **marketer** writes `release/listing.json` (status `RELEASING`). The listing is validated against store rules — blurb length and HTML, exactly 7 keywords, exactly 3 categories, no leftover placeholders — and the project is marked `RELEASED` when it passes, `FAILED` when it does not.
